{"page":542,"verses":[{"verse_key":"58:1","surah":58,"ayah":1,"ar_uthmani":" قَدْ سَمِعَ ٱللَّهُ قَوْلَ ٱلَّتِى تُجَـٰدِلُكَ فِى زَوْجِهَا وَتَشْتَكِىٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَٱللَّهُ يَسْمَعُ تَحَاوُرَكُمَآ ۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعٌۢ بَصِيرٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"God has heard the words of the woman who disputed with you [Prophet] about her husband and complained to God: God has heard what you both had to say. He is all hearing, all seeing.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"قَدْ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"qad","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":2,"ar":"سَمِعَ","en_gloss":"Allah has heard","transliteration":"samiʿa","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah has heard","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":4,"ar":"قَوْلَ","en_gloss":"(the) speech","transliteration":"qawla","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلَّتِى","en_gloss":"(of one) who","transliteration":"allatī","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":6,"ar":"تُجَـٰدِلُكَ","en_gloss":"disputes with you","transliteration":"tujādiluka","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":7,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"concerning","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":8,"ar":"زَوْجِهَا","en_gloss":"her husband","transliteration":"zawjihā","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَتَشْتَكِىٓ","en_gloss":"and she directs her complaint","transliteration":"watashtakī","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":10,"ar":"إِلَى","en_gloss":"to","transliteration":"ilā","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱللَّهِ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"And Allah","transliteration":"wal-lahu","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":13,"ar":"يَسْمَعُ","en_gloss":"hears","transliteration":"yasmaʿu","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":14,"ar":"تَحَاوُرَكُمَآ ۚ","en_gloss":"(the) dialogue of both of you","transliteration":"taḥāwurakumā","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":15,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":16,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":17,"ar":"سَمِيعٌۢ","en_gloss":"(is) All-Hearer","transliteration":"samīʿun","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":18,"ar":"بَصِيرٌ","en_gloss":"All-Seer","transliteration":"baṣīrun","verse_key":"58:1"},{"pos":19,"ar":"١","en_gloss":"(1)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"58:1"}]},{"verse_key":"58:2","surah":58,"ayah":2,"ar_uthmani":"ٱلَّذِينَ يُظَـٰهِرُونَ مِنكُم مِّن نِّسَآئِهِم مَّا هُنَّ أُمَّهَـٰتِهِمْ ۖ إِنْ أُمَّهَـٰتُهُمْ إِلَّا ٱلَّـٰٓـِٔى وَلَدْنَهُمْ ۚ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَيَقُولُونَ مُنكَرًا مِّنَ ٱلْقَوْلِ وَزُورًا ۚ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُورٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Even if any of you say to their wives, ‘You are to me like my mother’s back,’they are not their mothers; their only mothers are those who gave birth to them. What they say is certainly blameworthy and false, but God is pardoning and forgiving.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"Those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":2,"ar":"يُظَـٰهِرُونَ","en_gloss":"pronounce zihar","transliteration":"yuẓāhirūna","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِنكُم","en_gloss":"among you","transliteration":"minkum","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":4,"ar":"مِّن","en_gloss":"[from]","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":5,"ar":"نِّسَآئِهِم","en_gloss":"(to) their wives","transliteration":"nisāihim","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":6,"ar":"مَّا","en_gloss":"not","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":7,"ar":"هُنَّ","en_gloss":"they","transliteration":"hunna","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":8,"ar":"أُمَّهَـٰتِهِمْ ۖ","en_gloss":"(are) their mothers","transliteration":"ummahātihim","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":9,"ar":"إِنْ","en_gloss":"Not","transliteration":"in","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":10,"ar":"أُمَّهَـٰتُهُمْ","en_gloss":"(are) their mothers","transliteration":"ummahātuhum","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":11,"ar":"إِلَّا","en_gloss":"except","transliteration":"illā","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":12,"ar":"ٱلَّـٰٓـِٔى","en_gloss":"those who","transliteration":"allāī","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَلَدْنَهُمْ ۚ","en_gloss":"gave them birth","transliteration":"waladnahum","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":14,"ar":"وَإِنَّهُمْ","en_gloss":"And indeed, they","transliteration":"wa-innahum","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":15,"ar":"لَيَقُولُونَ","en_gloss":"surely say","transliteration":"layaqūlūna","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":16,"ar":"مُنكَرًۭا","en_gloss":"an evil","transliteration":"munkaran","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":17,"ar":"مِّنَ","en_gloss":"[of]","transliteration":"mina","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":18,"ar":"ٱلْقَوْلِ","en_gloss":"[the] word","transliteration":"l-qawli","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":19,"ar":"وَزُورًۭا ۚ","en_gloss":"and a lie","transliteration":"wazūran","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":20,"ar":"وَإِنَّ","en_gloss":"But indeed","transliteration":"wa-inna","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":21,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":22,"ar":"لَعَفُوٌّ","en_gloss":"(is) surely, Oft-Pardoning","transliteration":"laʿafuwwun","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":23,"ar":"غَفُورٌۭ","en_gloss":"Oft-Forgiving","transliteration":"ghafūrun","verse_key":"58:2"},{"pos":24,"ar":"٢","en_gloss":"(2)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"58:2"}]},{"verse_key":"58:3","surah":58,"ayah":3,"ar_uthmani":"وَٱلَّذِينَ يُظَـٰهِرُونَ مِن نِّسَآئِهِمْ ثُمَّ يَعُودُونَ لِمَا قَالُوا۟ فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مِّن قَبْلِ أَن يَتَمَآسَّا ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ تُوعَظُونَ بِهِۦ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Those of you who say such a thing to their wives, then go back on what they have said, must free a slave before the couple may touch one another again––this is what you are commanded to do, and God is fully aware of what you do––","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"And those who","transliteration":"wa-alladhīna","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":2,"ar":"يُظَـٰهِرُونَ","en_gloss":"pronounce zihar","transliteration":"yuẓāhirūna","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِن","en_gloss":"[from]","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":4,"ar":"نِّسَآئِهِمْ","en_gloss":"(to) their wives","transliteration":"nisāihim","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ثُمَّ","en_gloss":"then","transliteration":"thumma","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":6,"ar":"يَعُودُونَ","en_gloss":"go back","transliteration":"yaʿūdūna","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لِمَا","en_gloss":"on what","transliteration":"limā","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":8,"ar":"قَالُوا۟","en_gloss":"they said","transliteration":"qālū","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":9,"ar":"فَتَحْرِيرُ","en_gloss":"then freeing","transliteration":"fataḥrīru","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":10,"ar":"رَقَبَةٍۢ","en_gloss":"(of) a slave","transliteration":"raqabatin","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مِّن","en_gloss":"before","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":12,"ar":"قَبْلِ","en_gloss":"before","transliteration":"qabli","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":13,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"[that]","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":14,"ar":"يَتَمَآسَّا ۚ","en_gloss":"they touch each other","transliteration":"yatamāssā","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":15,"ar":"ذَٰلِكُمْ","en_gloss":"That","transliteration":"dhālikum","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":16,"ar":"تُوعَظُونَ","en_gloss":"you are admonished","transliteration":"tūʿaẓūna","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":17,"ar":"بِهِۦ ۚ","en_gloss":"to it","transliteration":"bihi","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":18,"ar":"وَٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"And Allah","transliteration":"wal-lahu","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":19,"ar":"بِمَا","en_gloss":"of what","transliteration":"bimā","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":20,"ar":"تَعْمَلُونَ","en_gloss":"you do","transliteration":"taʿmalūna","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":21,"ar":"خَبِيرٌۭ","en_gloss":"(is) All-Aware","transliteration":"khabīrun","verse_key":"58:3"},{"pos":22,"ar":"٣","en_gloss":"(3)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"58:3"}]},{"verse_key":"58:4","surah":58,"ayah":4,"ar_uthmani":"فَمَن لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ مِن قَبْلِ أَن يَتَمَآسَّا ۖ فَمَن لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَإِطْعَامُ سِتِّينَ مِسْكِينًا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِتُؤْمِنُوا۟ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ ۚ وَتِلْكَ حُدُودُ ٱللَّهِ ۗ وَلِلْكَـٰفِرِينَ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"but anyone who does not have the means should fast continuously for two months before they touch each other, and anyone unable to do this should feed sixty needy people. This is so that you may [truly] have faith in God and His Messenger. These are the bounds set by God: grievous torment awaits those who ignore them.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"فَمَن","en_gloss":"Then whoever","transliteration":"faman","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":2,"ar":"لَّمْ","en_gloss":"(does) not","transliteration":"lam","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":3,"ar":"يَجِدْ","en_gloss":"find","transliteration":"yajid","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":4,"ar":"فَصِيَامُ","en_gloss":"then fasting","transliteration":"faṣiyāmu","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":5,"ar":"شَهْرَيْنِ","en_gloss":"(for) two months","transliteration":"shahrayni","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":6,"ar":"مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ","en_gloss":"consecutively","transliteration":"mutatābiʿayni","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":7,"ar":"مِن","en_gloss":"before","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":8,"ar":"قَبْلِ","en_gloss":"before","transliteration":"qabli","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":9,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"[that]","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":10,"ar":"يَتَمَآسَّا ۖ","en_gloss":"they both touch each other","transliteration":"yatamāssā","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":11,"ar":"فَمَن","en_gloss":"But (he) who","transliteration":"faman","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":12,"ar":"لَّمْ","en_gloss":"not","transliteration":"lam","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":13,"ar":"يَسْتَطِعْ","en_gloss":"is able","transliteration":"yastaṭiʿ","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":14,"ar":"فَإِطْعَامُ","en_gloss":"then (the) feeding","transliteration":"fa-iṭ'ʿāmu","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":15,"ar":"سِتِّينَ","en_gloss":"(of) sixty","transliteration":"sittīna","verse_key":"58:4"},{"pos":1